#
# Counter-example for the NATIVE math:UnliftableIngest gate (crates/validate structural_lint,
# NOT a SHACL shape — the conformance runner reaches it through its structural-lint channel,
# and ex:ecIngestRunUnliftable pins the isolation). A bridge run RETAINS its source witness through
# math:parseSource and carries the full grounding frame (logic:instantiatesSchema /
# logic:instantiatesPlan and its lift correspondence math:ingestCorrespondence), so it
# passes math:IngestRunShape and is NOT math:UngroundedIngestRun — yet it produces NO
# structured math: codomain: nothing is gmeow:wasGeneratedBy it. The put leg silently
# dropped everything it was meant to lift, which is exactly the produced-nothing case the
# native gate rejects (a bridge lifts fully or hard-fails, never emits a degraded/empty lift).
# Exercised by the crates/validate lint test unliftable_ingest_fires_when_run_produces_no_codomain.
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:run a math:RIngestRun ;
    math:parseSource ex:srcWitness ;
    logic:instantiatesSchema ex:schema ;
    logic:instantiatesPlan ex:plan ;
    math:ingestCorrespondence ex:corr .
# The witness retains its source verbatim, so the ONE thing wrong with this run is the
# empty codomain — a minimal violation stays minimal only if it is well-formed everywhere
# else, and a bare witness would add a second, unrelated defect (the amnesic case).
ex:srcWitness a math:MathematicalObject ; logic:loadBearing true ;
    math:retainedSource "fit <- lm(mpg ~ wt, data = mtcars)" .
ex:schema a logic:ActionSchema .
ex:plan a logic:Plan .
ex:corr a logic:Correspondence ;
    logic:morphismClass logic:LossyLens ;
    logic:mnemomorphic true .
